list.item:
Summary - an overview of the model's mathematics:
the name of its unit system and its units (Change... opens the Model Unit System tab);
how many parameters and functions it has, under the same headings as the Parameters and Functions table's Defined In choices (Global, Reactions and Rules, Applications), each broken down beneath (global parameters, species and structure sizes; reactions and reaction rules; each application);
and
the measured physical constants VCell's equations use, whose accepted values science refines over time (the Faraday constant, Avogadro's number, the gas constant and KMOLE), with their values and units in the model's unit system (All Predefined Expressions opens the Predefined Expressions tab).
Double-click a row of the counts, or choose it and click Show in Parameters and Functions, to list what it counts there; a row under Global or Reactions and Rules lists all of its heading's.
